meta {
  name: Install a skill (multipart, admin)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/skills
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(/absolute/path/to/a/skill.zip)
}

docs {
  Extracts a skill archive into `<workspace>/skills/<name>/`. Point `file` at a real .zip on
  disk (set `skillZip` in the environment and copy it here); the client sets the multipart
  boundary, so don't add a Content-Type header.

  Replacement is total — a re-upload removes the previous folder first, so a script the new
  version no longer mentions cannot survive to be run. QuickJoiner's stored configuration for
  that name is NOT reset: an admin's scope decision outlives the files.

  Admin only (403 otherwise). 400 with a stated reason when the archive is unreadable, has no
  SKILL.md, or exceeds the size/member bounds.
}
